      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tstd::ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n\tstd::cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n\tint n, s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\n\t// Allocate contiguous aligned memory for the matrix (row-major)\n\tint *matrix = static_cast<int*>(aligned_alloc(64, sizeof(int) * n * n));\n\tif (!matrix) {\n\t\tstd::cerr << \"Memory allocation failed\\n\";\n\t\treturn 1;\n\t}\n\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i * n + j]);\n\n\tassert(s < n);\n\tassert(n < 8000);\n\tassert(s > 0);\n\tassert(n > 0);\n\n\tlong long sum = 0;\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < s; ++i)\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum) aligned(matrix:64)\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < s; ++j)\n\t\t\tsum += matrix[i * n + j];\n\n\tlong long mxSum = sum;\n\n\tint dir = 1;\n\tint i = 0;\n\tint j = 0;\n\twhile (i + s <= n) {\n\t\tif ((j + s == n && dir == 1) || (j == 0 && dir == -1)) {\n\t\t\tconst int exitingRow = i;\n\t\t\tconst int enteringRow = exitingRow + s;\n\t\t\tif (enteringRow >= n)\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\t\tlong long sub_sum = 0, add_sum = 0;\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sub_sum,add_sum) aligned(matrix:64)\n\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\n\t\t\t\tsub_sum += matrix[exitingRow * n + j + k];\n\t\t\t\tadd_sum += matrix[enteringRow * n + j + k];\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsum -= sub_sum;\n\t\t\tsum += add_sum;\n\n\t\t\t++i;\n\t\t\tdir *= -1;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tconst int exitingCol = (dir == 1) ? j : j + s - 1;\n\t\t\tconst int enteringCol = (dir == 1) ? j + s : j - 1;\n\n\t\t\tlong long sub_sum = 0, add_sum = 0;\n#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sub_sum,add_sum) aligned(matrix:64)\n\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\n\t\t\t\tsub_sum += matrix[(i + k) * n + exitingCol];\n\t\t\t\tadd_sum += matrix[(i + k) * n + enteringCol];\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tsum -= sub_sum;\n\t\t\tsum += add_sum;\n\n\t\t\tj += dir;\n\t\t}\n\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n\tfree(matrix);\n\treturn 0;\n}",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining the two separate subtract and add loops into a single SIMD reduction loop with two accumulators reduces loop overhead and improves vectorization efficiency, while preserving correctness. Adding alignment hints further aids auto-vectorization.",
  "notes": "Replaced each pair of #pragma omp simd reduction(-:sum) / reduction(+:sum) loops with one combined loop using separate sub_sum and add_sum reductions, then updating sum outside the loop. Added aligned(matrix:64) to all SIMD pragmas for better code generation.",
